[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_1]
Jahr Null

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_1_desc]
“Since the beginning of the ‘Year Zero’, Equestria will become a land of order, peace and prosperity.” - “The Great Joint Declaration of Empress Cozy, Queen Chrysalis and Lord Tirek”
December 24th, 1002, the Hearth’s Warming Eve, the Big Three reunited in Canterlot. They exchanged views on the management of their respective territories in the past three years, and discussed ways to ease border disputes, jointly combat terrorist organizations, protect food security for all parties, and they exchanged views on many issues of concern to the three parties, including addressing climate change. The meeting reiterated that the three tribes of ponies, changelings and centaurs will remain unswerving in their friendship, adhere to the spirit of the Canterlot Pact, and move towards a better future together.
It is worth noting that addressing climate change has become an emerging yet very important topic at this meeting: since the end of the Ultimate Battle, the Windigos have been hovering over Equestria for three years, and the global cooling it has caused has had a large impact on the world. The production and life of various creatures pose serious challenges. Coinciding with the Hearth’s Warming Festival, Empress Cozy Glow pointed out: “The Hearth’s Warming Festival originated from the initiative of the ponies. The original intention was to promote the concept of unity and cooperation in order to fight against the Windigos. Practice has shown that the Hearth’s Warming Festival did not achieve the desired goal of unity against the Windigos. On the contrary, it has instead become a tool for many old-harmonism forces, led by Starlight Glimmer, to attack the legitimacy of the Equestria Empire’s government.” Empress Cozy Glow then proposed to cancel the Hearth’s Warming Festival and replace it with a new festival. Queen Chrysalis agreed with this proposal, saying: “The custom of changelings celebrating Hearth’s Warming Festival originated from the instigation of war criminal Twilight Sparkle. It is a cultural invasion to the changelings done by the ponies, and is not in line with the friendship between ponies and changelings, nor with the reality of ponies and changelings living together as equals.” Lord Tirek suggested that the new holiday should be called “Year Zero” to commemorate that Equestria has entered a new era under the leadership of the Big Three. Lord Tirek also emphasized that the purpose of the holiday should be to enhance unity and emphasize safety. Empress Cozy Glow and Queen Chrysalis agreed.

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_1_o0]
Okay

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_1_o1]
Nonsense!

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_1_THREAT]
Cancellation of the Hearth’s Warming Festival

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_2]
Jahr Null Celebration

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_2_desc]
On Hearth’s Warming Day, the “Big Three” held a grand banquet, and after the banquet, the host Empress Cozy Glow announced the signing of the “Great Joint Declaration” by the “Big Three” (a.k.a. “The Great Joint Declaration by Empress Cozy Glow, Queen Rebuild, and Lord Tirek”), and announced that the new festival “Jahr Null” would replace the original Hearth’s Warming Day.
To demonstrate the cross-era nature of “Jahr Null” and the determination of the “Big Three” to maintain common security and stability, they jointly held a public trial of the war criminals left over from the Ultimate Battle. The trial process lasted for more than three hours and achieved the following results: six pony war criminals led by Twilight Sparkle, several changeling war criminals led by Thorax, were sentenced to death by bludgeoning; two former princesses of Equestria were sentenced to life imprisonment and will be detained in Tartarus Prison; six elders were sentenced to life imprisonment and will be detained in Canterlot Prison.
“Today, marks the beginning of Jahr Null — Year Zero! We will do away with the old! Today, history ends, and the future begins!”
The Jahr Null Celebration ended in thunderous applause.

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_2_o0]
Okay

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_2_o1]
R.I.P... Fluttershy...

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_2_o2]
R.I.P... Twilight Sparkle...

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_2_o3]
R.I.P... Friends...

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_2_o4]
Good!

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_2_o5]
Alas...

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_2_o6]
...

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_3]
Missing of the Pillars

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_3_desc]
According to the deputy captain of the Canterlot City Guard of the Equestria Empire, six prisoners detained in Canterlot: Starswirl, Meadowbrook, Magnus, Somnambula, Mistmane, and Rockhoof, escaped from Canterlot Prison yesterday and are currently missing. The Equestria Empire Guard reminds all Canterlot residents to remain vigilant, take precautions for their own safety, and report any suspicious behavior to the Empire Guard in a timely manner. At the same time, the Empire Guard also welcomes all ponies and creatures from all regions, including non-ponies, to actively provide information and assist in the capture of the six fugitives.

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_3_o0]
Emm...

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_4]
The Griffon Lies Heavy

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_4_desc]
After years of waiting, A.K. Yearling has finally released a new book in the Daring Do series: The Griffon Lies Heavy.
However, in a departure from her usual adventure style, this new book describes a unique story: Daring Do comes to a fantasy world where history is completely different from our world. In that fantasy world, M6 defeated the Big Three in that Ultimate Battle.
“It is a world full of harmony, a world that all ponies yearn for...” Yearling wrote in the book.
The Ministry of Order has declared that The Griffon Lies Heavy is prohibited, and has banned its printing and publishing. All ponies who own The Griffon Lies Heavy should turn it in within 7 days. The Ministry of Order has also issued a warrant for the arrest of A.K. Yearling.

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_4_o0]
Emm...

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_4_o1]
Emm...

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_5]
The Summer Sun Celebration

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_5_desc]
On June 21, the Equestria Empire held the first Summer Sun Celebration in Canterlot since Jahr Null. Representatives from all the territories of the Empire of Equestria came to attend the meeting.
At the opening ceremony of the celebration, the Empress of Friendship, Princess Cozy Glow made the first speech, summarizing the series of achievements made by the Empire in various fields since Jahr Null, looking forward to the future, and expressing the determination to eradicate the rebellion.
Later, the representative of the territories, the “Loyalist Medal” winner, the champion of the first “Empire Excellent Duchess Contest”, the Duchess of Ponyville, Trixie Lulamoon made her speech. Duchess Trixie reported to the Empress Cozy Glow the work since her appointment, praised the achievements of the Equestria Empire so far, and expressed her gratitude to Cozy Glow. The opening ceremony ended with the national anthem of the Equestria Empire, and the Summer Sun Celebration will continue for about a week.
However, according to the Mirror of Freedom Press’s report, the opening ceremony of the celebration was not as harmonious as it was shown to the outside world: Cozy Glow had repeatedly expressed her unwillingness to attend the Summer Sun Celebration, calling it “long and boring”. The Mirror of Freedom Press also captured several shots of Cozy Glow showing impatience during Duchess Trixie’s speech, and there were rumors that Cozy Glow did not trust Duchess Trixie.
The official radio station of the Resistance, the Red Radio, refused to comment on the Summer Sun Celebration. The spokespony of the Resistance said that the Resistance held its own Summer Sun Celebration in Our Town.
In addition to the ponies, in recent years, many other species including Yaks and Griffons have begun to celebrate the Summer Sun Celebration in their own way, and the world of Equestria is filled with a festive and peaceful atmosphere.

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_5_o0]
Okay

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_6]
Jahr Eins

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_6_desc]
A year has passed, and Empress Cozy Glow has once again held a celebration, but it is much smaller than before.
Ponies disagree on whether the Empire is getting better. Some say that nothing has changed, and the Windigos still circle in the sky; others say that Equestria is changing, undergoing a revolution, both technological and political; and of course, there are rumors that the smaller celebration has nothing to do with the situation of the Empire, but is simply the Empress’s own wish — she hates the social niceties of such events, and is tired of the trivialities of the ceremony.

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_6_o0]
Okay

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_7]
Imperial Finance Status Report by EEMF

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_7_desc]
According to the latest statistics from the Equestria Empire Ministry of Finance (EEMF), the Equestria Empire is in a serious deficit, and we will have to raise taxes again to cover the growing expenditures. The main expenditures include: the cost of the Windigo disaster, domestic security costs, foreign war and diplomatic expenses, royal luxury goods and celebration expenses, etc.

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_7_o0]
Okay

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_8]
Imperial Security Status Report by EEMO

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_8_desc]
According to the latest statistics from the Equestria Empire Ministry of Order (EEMO), since the tax increase last month, the number of organized anti-imperial political crimes in the central jurisdiction of the Equestria Empire has increased significantly. The increase in taxes has aroused considerable dissatisfaction among many ponies, and many slogans that do not respect the Empress have begun to spread among the people...

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_8_o0]
Strict Suppression!

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_9]
“Imitator Movement” Report by EEMO

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_9_desc]
The strict suppression seems to have backfired... The “Imitator Movement” is now spreading rapidly in the central jurisdiction of the Equestria Empire. Irony has replaced direct insult. Many ponies begin to imitate the slogan of the Empress, and sarcastically praise the Empress. Even began to imitate the Empress’s dress, and uglify the image of the Empress...

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_9_o0]
Emm... Stricter Suppression!

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_10]
Canterlot Anti-Tax Incident

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_10_desc]
Since July 12th, a large number of ponies have gathered in Canterlot to protest the tax increase by the Equestria Empire. Despite the large number of police and military forces dispatched by the central government of the Equestria Empire, many bloody incidents have occurred, and the ponies gathered in Canterlot have not been dispersed. On July 14th, the ponies tried to rush into and destroy Canterlot Prison. In the end, the ponies were still dispersed.
Empress Cozy Glow expressed extreme anger at this incident and will launch a rapid and in-depth investigation to bring all the masterminds to justice. Regarding the controversial policy of raising taxes, the Empire has not made a clear statement, but the reports of the Empire Central Television seem to be trying to imply that this riot is not related to taxes, and that the changelings have infiltrated and incited chaos, and the ponies should be more concerned about foreign enemies than internal tax issues.
A series of announcements from the Empire Central announced that the incident was over, but there is evidence that, as the direct riots of the residents were suppressed, the “imitator movement” began to rise in popularity among the people, and the ponies began to express their dissatisfaction through imitation rather than opposition to Empress Cozy Glow, through ambiguous praise rather than insults.

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_10_o0]
Only The Tides Are Forever

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_10_o1]
Damn Cozy... Oh no, I didn’t mean...

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_10_THREAT]
Only The Tides Are Forever

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_11]
Canterlot Explosion Incident

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_11_desc]
“Everypony is born to be and should remain to be free and equal.” - Anonymous “Imitator Movement” member.
On August 26th, a shocking event occurred: Canterlot Train Station was attacked by explosives. At the same time, a videotape was sent to various media outlets. In the videotape, an “Imitator” dressed as Empress Cozy Glow incited the public to join her uprising on November 5th, and claimed that she would “kill Cozy Glow” on November 5th. The videotapes received by various media outlets were quickly confiscated by the official government of the Equestria Empire, but the videotapes were still made public by the “Mirror of Freedom”.
The Equestria Empire Ministry of Order issued several regulations, requiring the public to refrain from discussing the so-called “November 5th Uprising”, prohibiting “Imitator” behavior, and stipulating that all ponies are obliged to report ponies involved in the “Imitator Movement”. The Ministry of Order has marked the anonymous pony in the videotape as the highest level of wanted, and will mobilize more police force than ever before to find and arrest the target.

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_11_o0]
Emm...

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_11_o1]
Security!

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_11_THREAT]
Canterlot Explosion Incident

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_12]
C for Cozy Glow

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_12_desc]
On November 5th, the uprising day claimed by the “Imitator”, the “Imitator” announced that he would “kill Cozy Glow” on this day... Under the coordination of the Ministry of Order, the Royal Guard of the Equestria Empire has been on alert and curfew for a month, and the Ministry of Defence has also deployed some troops to station in the Canterlot city center and surrounding areas. Since November 4th, the Canterlot city center has been completely closed.
The uprising day finally arrived, a large number of “Imitators” dressed as Cozy Glow appeared in major cities of the Equestria Empire. The police and army in the Canterlot city center used force against the “Imitators” who refused to obey orders according to the orders... It was a night that will be remembered forever.
At midnight on November 6th, the bell rang, and Cozy Glow’s personal TV speech ended the prophecy of “killing Cozy Glow”. Under the suppression of the police and army, the “Imitators” in various cities quickly dispersed.
The Equestria Empire has returned to its former peace, but in the center of the vortex—the Canterlot city center square, the police have not been able to clean up the “Cozy Glow” bodies left on the square last night. In a sense, the prophecy was successful—on November 5th, “Cozy Glow” was killed, not by the rebels, but by the Imperial police and the Imperial army.

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_12_o0]
Emm...

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_12_o1]
How could this even happen?!

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_13]
Magiae Naturalis Principia Mathematica

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_13_desc]
Recently, a new book published by the Free Equestria has caused quite a stir in the academic world. At a symposium in the Free Equestria, the discussion of the nature of magic has attracted the attention of Sunset Shimmer, who then handed the question over to Twilight Sparkle from the human world. After a period of research, combined with the knowledge of the magic of Equestria and the technology of the human world, Twilight Sparkle proposed a new systematic theory of magic and wrote it into the book “Magiae Naturalis Principia Mathematica”.
The book states that a spell consists of two parts: charging and weaving. The charging of magic determines the strength of the spell’s effect, such as suspending a stone or lifting a mountain. The charging ability depends on the talent of the caster and long-term endurance training. The weaving of the spell changes the form of the magic, such as creating a teacup or a piece of cake. The weaving of the spell depends on imagination and the understanding and learning of spells. The book does not elaborate on the conservation of magic energy and the medium problem. Nevertheless, the “Principia” is epoch-making, and many ponies believe that it will open up a whole new field of research.
It is said that Twilight Sparkle was inspired by a mistake in using magic when she was hit by an apple thrown by Applejack. However, some critics believe that Twilight Sparkle may have simply plagiarized similar views of Starswirl. In response to this controversy, Twilight Sparkle said, “If I can see further, it is because I am standing on the shoulders of the Pillar.”

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_13_o0]
Emm...

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_13_o1]
Good!

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_14]
Crystal Faire

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_14_desc]
The Crystal Empire annual event - Crystal Faire, is held today at the Crystal Square. Due to the wars and various matters in the past few years, the scale of the Crystal Faire has been greatly reduced, and the scale of this year’s Crystal Faire has almost returned to the pre-war level: martial arts, flag parade, music, food, everything. The Crystal Empire — this ancient Empire has never let the ponies down, always full of vitality and vitality.

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_14_o0]
Okay

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_15]
Ponyville’s Harsh Winter

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_15_desc]
According to meteorologists’ forecast, due to the influence of the Windigos, even though the weather factory and the weather lab have reduced the snowmaking capacity to 30% of the original, Ponyville will still face an unprecedented harsh winter.
Thanks to the agricultural reform during Mayor Mare’s tenure, Ponyville is now mainly growing cold-resistant crops, but this harsh winter will still have a huge impact on the lives of Ponyville residents.
Due to the large reduction in the number of apple trees compared to three years ago, and the longer growth cycle of apple trees, we have exhausted all the wood in store. This means that this winter we will lack enough wood to keep warm.
Therefore, agricultural experts suggest that a new forest logging plan should be implemented immediately, and more fast-growing forests should be planted so that there will be enough wood to keep warm for future winters.

[en.EVENT_TIMELINE_15_o0]
Okay

